30,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found out that some rooms are way colder than others, and paying a fixed seasonal rate makes people feel much more relaxed about using the heat!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The bills fluctuate wildly—February is triple August. Also, installing individual meters would be very expensive, costing 34,000 yen per room plus maintenance.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Rin,,Both the templates and the room-metering I looked into seem like a lot of work. It takes forever to log everything and calculate who owes what.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"My suspicions were right. Some rooms use four times more power than others. Also, our payment history is a mess because people keep questioning the totals.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"It's worse than I thought. People are paying late because they're arguing, and some even suffered in the heat just to avoid the conflict of a pooled bill.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, if meters are too expensive, maybe a fixed rate is better? It stops us from worrying every time we flip a switch.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"A fixed rate avoids the monthly stress, but we'd still have to settle the difference at the end of the year. It's more stable than our current chaos.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mio, as long as the ""settling"" doesn't take all night! If we do a fixed rate, can we make the final calculation simple?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Misaki, the fact that people are avoiding the cooler shows the current system is failing. We need a method that removes the ""who is using what"" argument.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"I agree, Shunichi. We need a system that stops the accusations. If we can't afford meters, we need a rule that everyone accepts without questioning.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Mio,,I really hate the idea of sitting in a coat in my own home. A seasonal fixed rate sounds like it would make the house feel warmer.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"From a cost perspective, the upfront price of meters is too high. A flat share is simple, but it doesn't solve the fairness issue Shunichi mentioned.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Rin,,"If we go with a flat share, it's the easiest to manage. But if we do a seasonal rate, who has to do the math at the end of the year?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A flat share is the most ""fair"" in terms of effort, but it ignores the fact that some of us use way more power. However, it's better than arguing.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"I think we should prioritize peace. Whether it's a flat share or a seasonal rate, the goal is to stop the monthly disputes and the late payments.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Mio,,I'm voting for the seasonal rate! It sounds the most comfortable for everyone.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I'll consider the options. We need to balance the upfront cost, the monthly volatility, and the administrative burden.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm leaning towards the flat share because it sounds like the least amount of work for whoever has to manage the money.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm torn between the flat share for simplicity and the meters for actual fairness, but the cost of meters is a dealbreaker.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I just want the tension to go away. A flat share is the most transparent and least likely to cause a fight over ""who used the heater.""","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
